Text 2: Soil chemist Nowsherwan Ali counters that on the clay-heavy fields he studies, standing residue keeps the surface so wet and cold each spring that nitrogen mineralization begins two weeks late, costing more yield than the added moisture is worth.', 'Based on the texts, how would Ali most likely respond to Ferro?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "He would point out that Ferro''s farms are too small to matter statistically."}, {"id": "B", "text": "He would agree that standing residue raises winter moisture but argue that on wet clay soils that same moisture delays spring nitrogen release and lowers yields."}, {"id": "C", "text": "He would dispute that residue affects soil moisture at all, since his fields are clay."}, {"id": "D", "text": "He would insist that residue be chopped and incorporated regardless of results."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hdsat-open-core-2026', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank', 'CC-BY-4.0', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank (CC-BY-4.0)', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, status = EXCLUDED.status, updated_at = NOW();
Text 2: Orthopedic data analyst Jena Fox replies that in her system''s log, falls cluster at the midnight-to-2 a.m. shift handover, when two different teams each assume the other has done hourly rounds.', 'Based on the texts, how would Fox most likely respond to Haddad?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "By disputing that medication walks occur at 5:30 a.m. at all."}, {"id": "B", "text": "By citing her handover-hour data to argue that midnight checks would catch the falls Haddad''s own timing analysis might miss."}, {"id": "C", "text": "By agreeing that both 5:30 and midnight rounds are worthless investments."}, {"id": "D", "text": "By proposing that fall prevention shifts entirely to the morning shift."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hdsat-open-core-2026', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank', 'CC-BY-4.0', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank (CC-BY-4.0)', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, status = EXCLUDED.status, updated_at = NOW();
In a study of prescribed low-intensity woodland burns, ecologist Mara Vance argues that spring burns maximize understory wildflower diversity. According to ecologist Mara Vance, expanding this practice across comparable sites would yield immediate, measurable gains.

Text 2
Evaluating the same prescribed low-intensity woodland burns, forester Jian Zhou observes that autumn burns better protect nesting canopy birds while still clearing dry fuel. Consequently, forester Jian Zhou cautions against adopting the practice without targeted safeguards.', 'Based on the texts, how would forester Jian Zhou most likely respond to ecologist Mara Vance''s view of prescribed low-intensity woodland burns?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "By arguing that prescribed low-intensity woodland burns should be abandoned immediately in all circumstances."}, {"id": "B", "text": "By acknowledging the potential benefit of prescribed low-intensity woodland burns while pointing out an unintended consequence that requires design or timing adjustments."}, {"id": "C", "text": "By claiming that ecologist Mara Vance''s measurements were fabricated without field testing."}, {"id": "D", "text": "By agreeing that prescribed low-intensity woodland burns produces no measurable side effects whatsoever."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hdsat-open-core-2026', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank', 'CC-BY-4.0', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank (CC-BY-4.0)', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, status = EXCLUDED.status, updated_at = NOW();
