• Cultures kept under constant light lose their circadian bioluminescence rhythm within four days.', 'The student wants to explain how bioluminescence protects Lingulodinium polyedra in two distinct ways. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Lingulodinium polyedra emits 100-millisecond flashes at a wavelength of 475 nanometers when mechanically agitated."}, {"id": "B", "text": "When disturbed by grazing copepods, Lingulodinium polyedra emits blue flashes that both directly startle the copepods—cutting feeding by 55%—and expose the grazers to nocturnal predatory fish."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Laboratory cultures of Lingulodinium polyedra lose their circadian rhythm if kept under constant illumination for four days."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Nocturnal predatory fish can spot illuminated prey from distances of up to two meters in dark water."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hdsat-open-core-2026', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank', 'CC-BY-4.0', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank (CC-BY-4.0)', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, status = EXCLUDED.status, updated_at = NOW();
