• Cultures kept under constant light lose their circadian bioluminescence rhythm within four days.', 'The student wants to contrast the ecological function of the flashes in the wild with a vulnerability observed under artificial laboratory conditions. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Researchers used laboratory shear-flow experiments to measure the duration of Lingulodinium polyedra flashes."}, {"id": "B", "text": "While Lingulodinium polyedra''s blue flashes deter copepod grazing by 55% in nocturnal marine environments, the organism loses this circadian bioluminescence rhythm within four days if exposed to constant laboratory light."}, {"id": "C", "text": "A single 100-millisecond flash at 475 nanometers can make a copepod visible to predatory fish two meters away."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Both copepods and nocturnal fish respond to the blue light emitted by marine dinoflagellates."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hdsat-open-core-2026', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank', 'CC-BY-4.0', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank (CC-BY-4.0)', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, status = EXCLUDED.status, updated_at = NOW();
• The ancient Greek theater at Epidaurus, built in the fourth century BCE, seats 14,000 spectators across 55 limestone rows.
• Acoustic measurements by Declercq and colleagues found that the corrugated limestone seat rows act as a diffraction grating.
• This stepped geometry suppresses background low-frequency wind and crowd murmur below 500 Hz.
• At the same time, it reflects high-frequency consonant sounds above 500 Hz toward the upper tiers without amplification.
• Modern reproductions built with smooth concrete steps fail to replicate this selective frequency filtering.', 'The student wants to explain how the seat geometry at Epidaurus improves speech intelligibility. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Declercq and colleagues conducted acoustic measurements at the ancient theater of Epidaurus."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Acting as an acoustic diffraction grating, Epidaurus''s 55 corrugated limestone rows suppress low-frequency background noise below 500 Hz while reflecting clear high-frequency speech sounds to the upper seats."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Modern theaters constructed with smooth concrete steps do not filter frequencies the way limestone rows do."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Built in the fourth century BCE, the Greek theater at Epidaurus seats 14,000 spectators across 55 rows."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hdsat-open-core-2026', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank', 'CC-BY-4.0', 'HDSAT Open Core Curated Bank (CC-BY-4.0)', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, status = EXCLUDED.status, updated_at = NOW();
